	<text xml:lang="la">
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>Salutem in [Christo]<note xml:id="fna" type="footnote" n="a"><hi>Hier und unten Textverlust durch Papierbeschädigung.</hi></note> Iesu!</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la">Postquam tanta rerum optimarum <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>mutatio t[am rep]ente <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>contigerit, non potui quin tecum <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>communcarem, <persName ref="p495">Bullingere</persName> amice et domine charissime, quae <lb xml:id="p1z5"/>mala imminent ecclesiae <placeName ref="l822">Germanicae</placeName>.</s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">Hodie <placeName ref="l491">Argentinam</placeName> <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>venit veredarius<note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8">Vermutlich <persName ref="p8121">Christopher Mont</persName> dessen diplomatische Tätigkeit in <placeName ref="l822">Deutschland</placeName> für <persName ref="p8375">König Heinrich VIII.</persName> in der damaligen Zeit belegt ist; s. Esther <hi>Hildebrandt,</hi> Christopher Mont, Anglo-German Diplomat, in: Sixteenth Century Journal XV/3, 1984, 281-292.</note> regius <placeName ref="l830">Angliae</placeName>, qui pridie quam scri<lb xml:id="p1z7"/>berentur haec reliquit castra caesareana atque ipsum <lb xml:id="p1z8"/>caesarem<note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" n="9"><persName ref="p18538">Karl V.</persName></note> apud <placeName ref="l1324">Heilbrunnen</placeName> in <placeName ref="l572">Wittenbergensi</placeName> terra<note xml:id="fn10" type="footnote" n="10"><placeName ref="l1324">Heilbronn</placeName>, <placeName ref="l572">Württemberg</placeName>; s. dazu <ref target="file12769">Nr. 2722</ref>, <ptr target="qvfn16411-9" type="qv"/>.</note>.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z9"/>Is refert caesarem mire elatum victoria atque <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>praeter solitum hillarem; nam audivisse se rebelles vocare <lb xml:id="p1z11"/>hos qui sese ultro dediderunt."</s>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">Licet," inquit, "<lb xml:id="p1z12"/>rebelles estis, tamen, quam sim misericors, ostendam."</s>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z13"/>Hęc verba fuere caesaris civitatis alicuius maiestratib<lb xml:id="p1z14"/>us<note xml:id="fnb" type="footnote" n="b"><hi>In der Vorlage</hi> maiestratui.</note> qui se dediderunt.</s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">Addit ad haec ne verbum <lb xml:id="p1z15"/>quidem de religione habere, atque solum pecuniae <lb xml:id="p1z16"/>mulctam iis inscribere, callide nimirum, ne vi<lb xml:id="p1z17"/>deatur sibi contrarius esse.</s>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la">Verum si conceditur, ut <lb xml:id="p1z18"/>universam <placeName ref="l822">Germaniam</placeName> superet, haud dubie ostendet, <lb xml:id="p1z19"/>quam sit callidus.</s>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la">Caeterum timor eius inva<lb xml:id="p1z20"/>sit univeram hanc terram circum <placeName ref="l491">Argentinam</placeName> ia<lb xml:id="p1z21"/>centem, neque quicquam quam obsidionem sperat <lb xml:id="p1z22"/>haec civitas.</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la">Comes item <persName ref="p7459">de Buren</persName><note xml:id="fn11" type="footnote" n="11"><persName ref="p7459">Maximilian von Egmont</persName>, Graf von <placeName ref="l2126">Büren</placeName>.</note> civitatulam <lb xml:id="p1z23"/>prope <placeName ref="l157">Francofordiam</placeName> langraviae<note xml:id="fn12" type="footnote" n="12"><persName ref="p3590">Philipp von Hessen</persName>.</note> occupavit, <placeName ref="l1779">Bermstat</placeName><note xml:id="fn13" type="footnote" n="13">Richtig: <placeName ref="l1779">Darmstadt</placeName>. - Dies war am 22. Dezember geschehen; s. <ref target="file12753">Nr. 2706</ref>, <ptr target="qvfn16394-1" type="qv"/>.</note>, <lb xml:id="p1z24"/>ni fallor, vocatam.</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la">Haec de <placeName ref="l822">Germania</placeName>.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div2" corresp="regest2">
				<p>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la">De <lb xml:id="p1z25"/><placeName ref="l830">Anglia</placeName> nobis refert is nuntius aeque iucunda atque <lb xml:id="p1z26"/>haec sunt tristia; nempe fuisse ducem aliquem, <lb xml:id="p1z27"/>cuius imperium in septemtrionem <placeName ref="l830">Angliae</placeName> tendebat, <lb xml:id="p1z28"/>vulgariter dux de <placeName ref="l722">Nordvolk</placeName><note xml:id="fn14" type="footnote" ana="bio" n="14"><persName ref="p7574">Thomas Howard</persName>, Duke of <placeName ref="l722">Norfolk</placeName> (gest. 25. August 1554). - Er und sein Sohn (s. unten <ptr target="qvfn16422-1" type="qv"/>) wurden im <placeName ref="l296">Londoner</placeName> Tower (Turm) am 12. Dezember 1546 gesteckt.</note> nuncupatus, hostis <lb xml:id="p1z29"/>infensissimus verbo dei, qui tentabat cum filio<note xml:id="fn15" type="footnote" n="15"><persName ref="p20134">Henry Howard</persName>, Earl of <placeName ref="l771">Surrey</placeName>. Er wurde am 19. Januar 1547 hingerichtet.<ptr target="zfnfn16422-1" type="zfn"/></note> et aliis <lb xml:id="p1z30"/>regnum papae et monachorum clam restituere.</s>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la">Verum <lb xml:id="p1z31"/>consilium eorum patet, et dux cum filio incarceratur.</s>
					<s n="14" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z32"/>Neque quicquam deest, quam unus <placeName ref="l553">Wintoniensis</placeName><note xml:id="fn16" type="footnote" n="16"><persName ref="p7497">Stephen Gardiner</persName>, Bischof von <placeName ref="l553">Winchester</placeName> (gest. 12. November 1555).</note>, qui nisi <lb xml:id="p1z33"/>item capiatur, res evangelica restitui non potest.</s>
					<s n="15" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z34"/>Oremus igitur dominum, ut ecclesiam suam undique oppressam <lb xml:id="p1z35"/>tueatur.</s>
					<s n="16" xml:lang="la">Haec tibi scribenda duxi.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div3" corresp="regest3">
				<p>
					<s n="17" xml:lang="la">Ego re<lb xml:id="p1z36"/>cta hinc, domino duce, tendam versus mare.</s>
					<s n="18" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell">Bene <lb xml:id="p1z37"/>vale.</s>
					<s n="19" xml:lang="la">Uxori<note xml:id="fn17" type="footnote" n="17"><persName ref="p20138">Adelheit Knüpli</persName>.</note> scripsi, quam, ut soleris et con<lb xml:id="p1z38"/>sulas me absente, oro.</s>
					<s n="20" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l491">Argentinae</placeName>, pridie kalendas <lb xml:id="p1z39"/>ianuarias 1546.<note xml:id="fn18" type="footnote" n="18">Dass damit nicht etwa der 31. Dezember 1545 gemeint ist, geht aus den in diesem Brief enthaltenen Angaben hervor.</note></s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="21" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z40"/>Tuus <persName ref="p505">Burcherus</persName>, <placeName ref="l830">Anglus</placeName>.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div4" corresp="regest4">
				<p>
					<s n="22" xml:lang="la" ana="salute"><lb xml:id="p1z41"/>D. <persName ref="p1548">Ricardus</persName><note xml:id="fn19" type="footnote" n="19"><persName ref="p1548">Richard Hilles</persName>.</note> cum uxore<note xml:id="fn20" type="footnote" ana="bio" n="20"><persName ref="p5231">Anna, geb. Lacey</persName>.</note> te et coniugem<note xml:id="fn21" type="footnote" ana="bio" n="21"><persName ref="p8051">Anna, geb. Adlischwyler</persName>.</note> plurimum sa<lb xml:id="p1z42"/>lutant.</s>
					<s n="23" xml:lang="la">Filiamque<note xml:id="fn22" type="footnote" n="22">Unbekannt.</note> ante septimanas plus minus sex acce<lb xml:id="p1z43"/>perunt, eaque revaluit ex puerperio.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Adresse auf der Rückseite:]</note>
					<s n="24" xml:lang="la"><pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>D. <persName ref="p495">Heinrico Bullingero</persName>, <lb xml:id="p2z2"/><placeName ref="l587">Tigurinae</placeName> ecclesiae pas<lb xml:id="p2z3"/>tori vigilantissimo, amico <lb xml:id="p2z4"/>et domino suo charissimo.</s>
					<s n="25" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p2z5"/><placeName ref="l587">Tiguri</placeName>.</s>
				</p>
